    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0536" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.918/10–445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-04T19:00:00-05:00">October 4, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1398. From Braden. Have just been informed by <hi rendition="#italic">Time</hi>
                    Magazine that while sales on newsstands in Buenos Aires of October 1st issue
                    have been permitted, distribution through post office (which constitutes major
                    portion of circulation) has been stopped by Government.</p>
                <p>This is in direct violation of Mexico City obligations and of agreement Lomuto
                    made with me on approximately June 13.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d382-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Please protest this further violation. [Braden.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="34" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram 1236, June 13, from Buenos Aires, <ref target="#pg507">p.
                    507</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
